\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TDOclminusPERSPRO2
\item[* relevant examples:] ver ella $\rightarrow$  ver la, 
                            saludar ellos $\rightarrow$  saludar los/les,
                            comprar \'{e}l $\rightarrow$  comprar lo
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] TC\_cliticrules
\item[* date of creation:] 10-JAN-1989 
\item[* author:] Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] TDOclminusPERSPRO
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 17/01/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
changed subrule models. added except for [forma].\\
WARNING: this rule is not reversible; analytically the NP-node is not 
recovered!
\item date: 15/10/90\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo/Elena Pinillos\\
Changed conditions to avoid DO-IO-clitics order. Added new rules to account for
the missing cases.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To create a corresponding DO-clitic when the DO is a PERSPRO;
the PERSPRO is deleted. The DO can have either Prepositive case (i.e. "a"
would have been inserted later) or Accusative case. For infinite cluses; glue 
rules follow.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
- This transformation is applicable for both Prepositive case (for which also
TDOclplusPERSPRO is applicable, i.e. the DO-PERSPRO can be either deleted or 
not) and for Accusative case (for which only this
transformation is applicable, i.e. the DO-PERSPRO h\'{a}s to be deleted).\\ \\
- No specification of mu4 and mu6 and mu10 is given yet. 
This will be necessary if an analytical component for Spanish is added.
\end{description}

